#: includes/class-gatecha-admin.php:136
msgid "Determines how forms behave if the GateCHA server cannot be reached. \"Fail closed\" is safer but may block legitimate users during an outage."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-gatecha-admin.php:148
msgid "Auto Verify"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-gatecha-admin.php:154
msgid "Automatically start verification when the user focuses the form. When disabled, the user must click the checkbox manually."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-gatecha-admin.php:166
msgid "Hide Branding"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-gatecha-admin.php:172
msgid "Hide the ALTCHA logo and \"Protected by ALTCHA\" footer. Keeping branding visible is recommended."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-gatecha-admin.php:181
msgid "Interaction Signals"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-gatecha-admin.php:183
msgid "Proof-of-work proves a browser did the work. It does not prove a human filled the form in. Interaction signals add a second opinion: how the form was filled, as counts and durations only. Never what was typed, never pointer coordinates, never an IP address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-gatecha-admin.php:184
msgid "Requires GateCHA 0.7.0 or later. Scores show up on your dashboard under HIS Monitor."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-gatecha-admin.php:197
msgid "Collect Interaction Signals"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-gatecha-admin.php:203
msgid "Load the collector from your GateCHA instance and send the aggregates along with each verification. On its own this changes nothing about who gets through: scores are recorded, never enforced."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-gatecha-admin.php:215
msgid "Reject Suspected Automation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-gatecha-admin.php:221
msgid "Fail verification when GateCHA flags a submission as automated. Needs the setting above. Turn it on once you have watched your own scores for a few days: a false positive here is silent, the visitor simply cannot submit and never tells you."
msgstr ""

